					<p class="body1" align="left"><span class="body1 style73"> <h2>News archive</h2><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-26 | Thursday</font></strong><br><br>Did you hear? <strong>Common Market</strong> is making moves on the radio charts, debuting at #2 on the CMJ underground hip-hop chart last week and holding #8 down this week with the likes of Lupe Fiasco and The Roots (big up to NW brethren <strong>Smoke from Oldominion</strong> also charting). A good look for Massline and the 206 - hopefully the rest of the country will stop sleeping and get the late pass on all the good music coming from our neck of the wilderness.<br />                       <br />Right in time for the November elections, the <strong>prez signed a bill today to authorize the construction of a fence along the US-Mexico border</strong>. Here&#39;s a video of <strong>Blue Scholars</strong> rocking the immigrant rights rally back in April with f news and first-hand footage of the massive mobilization:<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-25 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br>Whatup Massliners and good people? We&#39;re a week late with this one, but congrats to to the 360&#39;s own <strong>Xperience - </strong>one half of the group Step Cousins and the newest Oldominion representative - dropping his solo joint <strong>Soultree</strong> last week. Massline homie <strong>Gabriel Teodros</strong> and <strong>Good Medicine</strong> fam <strong>Macklemore</strong> were out in Olympia to support at the record release, and word is the show was bananas. <a href="http://www.myspace.com/xperience88" target="new">Go check Xperience&#39;s music and holler at an album at his <strong>myspace page</strong>. </a><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-23 | Monday</font></strong><br><br><strong>DJ Red Alert</strong>... is down with us... or just really curious about the Macbook Pro&#39;s built-in webcam. <br />
                      <br />
                      Healthy dialogue happening in where else but <strong>The Dialogue</strong> as well as the rest of the MassLine forums. The hottest topic this week? Not &quot;<a href="../smf/index.php?topic=115.0"><strong>really bad rap album covers&quot; </strong></a>or the passing of the <strong>Military Commissions act</strong>, but the <strong><a href="../smf/index.php?topic=117.0">VH1 Hip-hop Honors show</a></strong>.<br />
                      <br />
                      Stay tuned this week as we announce the dates and cities of the upcoming monumental <strong>MassLine Tour</strong>.
We&#39;ve already booked shows down the I-5 corridor, and we&#39;re currently
locking down a handful of inland dates on the trip back up to the 206. <br />
                      <br />
It&#39;ll be a minute before the next MassLine artist show (Common Market
&amp; Gabriel Teodros Nov 10 @ Chop Suey), so hold tight. If you&#39;re in
the Seattle area, check out what the good folks at <a href="http://www.obeseproductions.com/"><strong>Obese Productions</strong></a> are up to.<br />
                      <p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-18 | Wednesday</font></strong><br><br><p>yet another unusually warm and sunny fall day in seattle. i&#39;m not complaining at all, but i have a sneaking feeling we&#39;re going to pay for this warmth in some other way. and that&#39;s the inconvenient truth.</p>                      <p>first off, big up to people who have stopped smoking cigarettes and cut back on drinking coffee. sure, thugs drink coffee. in seattle. no disrespect to the sexy beast, but that stuff ain&#39;t good for you, son!</p>                     <p>i don&#39;t know how many folks out there are into the whole sneaker phenomenon that all the hipsters and 2nd-tier hipsters have suddenly &quot;discovered&quot; like shoes didn&#39;t exist before, like Jig wasn&#39;t stacking Nike&#39;s in &#39;89, but there&#39;s an <a href="http://www.scion.com/route/kicks_synopsis.html"><strong>independent film</strong></a> i&#39;m probably gonna hit up on Monday that explores the world of foot fashion in hip hop.</p>                     <p class="body1 style72">below is a clip that illustrates the need for our own media. big up to hari kondabolu for this one. </p> 					                     <p>&quot;yea the media is liberal. if you&#39;re a nazi.&quot;<br />                        -dan moore</p><p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><strong><font color="#333300" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif" size="2">2006-10-16 | Monday</font></strong><br><br>Peace                          to the good folks who witnessed <strong>Common Market</strong>                        hold it down at The Paramount last friday. If you missed                        it, you can catch CM at the Showbox this Thursday October                        19th headlining the Seattle Art Museum benefit with souls                        sista <strong>Choklate</strong> (who performs with Blue                          Scholars on November 22 @ The Showbox). <br />                       <br />                       Another good look for the 206 as the homegrown b-boy crew                        <a href="http://www.myspace.com/massivemonkees"><strong>Massive                        Monkees</strong></a> repped for the whole country in the                        <strong><a href="http://www.bboychampionships.com/lineup/crews.htm">UK                        Bboy World Finals</a></strong><a href="http://www.bboychampionships.com/lineup/crews.htm">.                          </a>They held the torch high all the way to the semi-finals                          before being stopped by eventual champion Pokemon Crew from                          France. Many who witnessed it say Massive was deserving                          of the title that night, if not a chance to be in the finals.                          Regardless, it&#39;s another testament to the talent and work                          ethic of folks right here in our own backyard. Word is also                          out that MM is featured on the <a href="../smf/index.php?topic=94.0"><strong>new                          XBox 360 ad.</strong></a><br />                       <br />                       Also, it was beautiful seeing the Seattle hip-hop scene                        stand up on Saturday in support of <strong>DV-One</strong>.                        <strong>Seaspot Magazine</strong> organized a photo shoot                          of well over 100 supporters at the Martin Luther King, Jr.                          memorial. Here&#39;s a <a href="http://myspace-516.vo.llnwd.net/01290/61/54/1290764516_l.jpg"><strong>preview                          shot</strong></a>, courtesy of <strong>Vivian Hsu</strong>.<br />                       <br />                       Be safe peoples.<p></p><br><hr align="center" noshade size="1" width="400"><br><center><div class="pagenumbers"><A HREF="archive.php?from=280">[&lt;&lt;]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=0">[1]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=5">[2]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=10">[3]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=15">[4]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=20">[5]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=25">[6]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=30">[7]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=35">[8]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=40">[9]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=45">[10]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=50">[11]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=55">[12]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=60">[13]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=65">[14]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=70">[15]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=75">[16]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=80">[17]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=85">[18]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=90">[19]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=95">[20]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=100">[21]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=105">[22]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=110">[23]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=115">[24]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=120">[25]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=125">[26]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=130">[27]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=135">[28]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=140">[29]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=145">[30]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=150">[31]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=155">[32]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=160">[33]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=165">[34]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=170">[35]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=175">[36]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=180">[37]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=185">[38]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=190">[39]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=195">[40]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=200">[41]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=205">[42]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=210">[43]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=215">[44]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=220">[45]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=225">[46]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=230">[47]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=235">[48]</A> <A HREF="archive.php?from=240">[49]</A> <A 